    <section class="reads" id="reads">
      <div class="wrap sh" data-r>
        <h2 class="slate">The model is your pick. The harness is the work.</h2>
        <p>Claude, Gemini and GPT all cut well once they know what’s in the film. So AgentShot puts its effort around the model: it measures your footage before it touches it, checks each change against the picture, and keeps every version. Swap the model per project; the harness stays.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="harness wrap" role="list">
        <li data-r style="--d:0"><b>Measures first</b><span>Words, voices, shots, the subject, the beat, loudness. On your computer or worker.</span></li>
        <li data-r style="--d:1"><b>Knows the craft</b><span>12 skills for motion design, walkthroughs, screen + facecam, Shorts, voice and music.</span></li>
        <li data-r style="--d:2"><b>Checks its work</b><span>Every change comes back as a before and after, never over your footage.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="scrolly" style={`--n:${log.length}`}>
        <div class="pin">
          <div class="panel paint" style={paint('grass', 'center', '#d6dfcc')}>
            <div class="paper sheet">
              <div class="tracks" aria-hidden="true">
                {log.map((r, i) => <button type="button" tabindex="-1" data-step={i}><span>{r.k}</span><i></i></button>)}
              </div>
              <div class="views" role="table" aria-label="What AgentShot measures, and what that lets you say">
                {log.map((r, i) => (
                  <div class="view" role="row" data-i={i}>
                    <span class="k" role="rowheader">{r.k}</span>
                    <div class="found" role="cell"><p class="lbl">What it found</p><p class="mono" set:html={r.found} /><span class="trace" set:html={r.trace} /></div>
                    <div class="say-it" role="cell"><p class="lbl">So you can say</p><q>{r.say}</q></div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="craft">And it knows the craft of the film you’re making: motion graphics, product walkthroughs, screen + facecam demos, talking heads, Shorts and Reels, promos and cleanup.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

